[0.000, "o", "\r\nStep 4/4: Running the agent to diagnose...\r\n"]
[97.128, "o", "\r\n=== Infra Whisperer Diagnosis ===\r\n\r\n✅ PR opened: **https://github.com/ccarrylab/infra-whisperer/pull/5**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📋 Final Incident Report\r\n\r\n### Active Incident: ALB Health Check Timeout → ECS Task Restart Loop\r\n**Severity:** High | **Started:** 2026-08-26 14:30 UTC | **Status:** Root cause identified, fix pending review\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Confidence-Ranked Hypotheses\r\n\r\n| Rank | Hypothesis | Confidence | Key Evidence |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **#1** | ECS service SG ingress rule mutated out-of-band, blocking ALB health checks | **~90%** | `\"Request timed out\"` in ECS events; app logs show HTTP 200; TF state SG description names the chaos mutation scenario |\r\n| **#2** | ALB health check misconfiguration (wrong path/port) | ~5% | Health check config (`GET /`, port 80) matches what the app serves |\r\n| **#3** | ECS task networking (subnet/IP assignment) | ~5% | `assign_public_ip=true`, correct subnets in TF state |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### What's Happening (Plain English)\r\nThe application servers are **completely he"]
[0.000, "o", "althy** — they're responding to requests every 10 seconds. But the load balancer's automated \"are you alive?\" checks are **timing out** before they can reach the servers. This is because the **network firewall rule** that allows the load balancer to talk to the servers was silently changed outside of our normal process. As a result, health checks are being dropped, the load balancer marks servers as dead, and ECS keeps restarting them in a loop — even though the app never actually crashed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Fix Proposed\r\n🔗 **PR #5** restores the correct firewall rule via Terraform. Once a human reviews and merges it, `terraform apply` will take ~30–45 seconds to clear the alarm. **No manual AWS console changes needed — and none recommended**, as that could cause further drift.\r\n"]
[0.160, "o", "\r\n=== Demo complete ===\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "To fix the real incident and restore service:\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "  cd terraform && terraform plan -out=tfplan && terraform apply tfplan\r\n\r\nTo tear down entirely and stop all AWS charges:\r\n  cd terraform && terraform destroy\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[7m%\u001b[27m\u001b[1m\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                 \r \r"]
